# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/
.swc

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# test/verification artifacts (Playwright test runner + MCP browser tool)
/test-results/
/.screenshots/
/.playwright-mcp/

# Cloud sync per-replica local state (manifest baseline + conflict log)
**/.cloud-sync-*

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.local.example
!.env.test.local.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.superpowers/

# Transient scheduled-task lock (per-session runtime artifact)
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# dev error log (runtime observability artifact — never commit)
/logs/

# Per-machine Claude Code settings (permission grants, local paths) — not shared
.claude/settings.local.json

/.cache/

# Agent working detritus (codex task output, session scratch)
.codex-tasks/
scratchpad/
dist/

# Python bytecode. scripts/codex-review.py imports scripts/codex-frontier-model.py, so a
# __pycache__/ appears under scripts/ on every review dispatch (PR #27).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# jest --json output, produced by CI for scripts/check-test-counts.py and handy locally.
jest-results.json

# Playwright auth state + seeded fixture for the cloud e2e (regenerated by the setup project)
playwright/.auth/

# Post-Plan Gate sentinel — transient, per-working-copy. Armed by
# .claude/hooks/check-plan-gate.sh, cleared at Post-Plan Gate 5/5.
.claude/plan-gate-pending

# Session-local execution state, armed by .claude/hooks/block-idle-stop.sh. Names the plan being
# executed and the last blocked step-count; both are per-machine, per-session. The PLAN's checkboxes
# are the durable, committed record of progress — these two files only decide when to interrupt.
.claude/executing-plan
.claude/executing-plan.state

# Session plans written by scripts/begin-plan.py. Deliberately NOT in docs/superpowers/plans/:
# that directory is the anchor registry's population (check-anchors.py globs it and requires a
# Goal + Anchor header on every dated file) and it is the durable design corpus. A session to-do
# list is neither — it is per-machine execution state, like the two sentinels above.
.claude/plans/

# Recall answers cached by scripts/recall-llm.py --arm, one file per plan. DERIVED from two things
# neither of which is committed: a `.claude/plans/` file (ignored just above) and the memory corpus
# under ~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory, which lives outside this repository entirely. So a cache
# here can be neither reproduced nor checked by anyone else, and `--arm` rewrites it whenever the
# plan's situations change. Ignored for the same reason as the plan it is keyed to.
.claude/recall-cache/

# Warn-only firings of scripts/check-banner-armed.py — one tab-separated line per turn that
# announced `## ▶ STEP i of N` with nothing armed. Per-machine evidence, not a shared record: it
# exists so the decision to promote that check from warning to blocking rests on a COUNT rather
# than an impression.
.claude/banner-warnings*.log
# F11 observations from the same guard (backlog #97). A SEPARATE file on purpose: the late flush
# is the ordinary case, so recording it in the warn log above would destroy `wc -l` as a count of
# warnings — which is that log's whole job. The glob above deliberately does not match this name.
.claude/banner-flush-observations.log

# Warn-only log from .claude/hooks/block-idle-stop.sh -> scripts/check-closing-table.py.
# Session-local evidence for whether that observer false-alarms; nothing parses it.
.claude/closing-table-warnings.log

# Which commit a CI watcher is armed for (scripts/check-ci-watched.py). SHA-scoped on purpose:
# a new push moves HEAD, the sentinel stops matching, and the check warns again. "Armed once,
# covered forever" is the bug it exists to catch, not the behaviour it should have.
.claude/ci-watching
# The CI observer's warn log — the evidence base for its false-alarm rate, session-local
# like its sibling `.claude/banner-warnings*.log` above. Added 2026-09-22.
.claude/ci-unwatched.log

# Generated pages never belong at the repo root. MEASURED 2026-08-30: `frag.html`
# and `rel-nested.html` — two rendered dashboards — were committed in 96ae502 by
# `git add -A`. They were written by the round-4 breach sweep, which applies every
# mutation entry INCLUDING the two whose whole point is a RELATIVE `--out` /
# `--fragment-only` path, and which did not pin its cwd. `--mutate .` itself is
# safe (`run_suite` uses `cwd=<temp copy>`); the hazard is an instrument run from
# the repo root. This is a backstop, not the fix — the fix is that instruments
# pin their cwd.
/*.html

# Per-session state written by scripts/check-banner-armed.py at every Stop (backlog #96).
# SESSION-LOCAL, never source: it churns on every stop, would conflict between branches,
# and carries session ids. It was tracked for exactly one commit by a `git add -A`.
.claude/banner-turn-state/

# ── Explainer pages (backlog #194) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `docs/explainers/` is TRACKED: the authored topic/brief pages have no source in git — the HTML
# IS the artifact, so losing it loses the work. `~/explainers` is symlinked here by
# `scripts/bootstrap-explainers.sh` so the server and the generators keep their hardcoded path.
#
# ⛔ BUT THE DERIVED PAGES MUST NOT BE TRACKED, and that is not a size argument. `gen-dashboard`,
# `gen-goals-page`, `gen-backlog-page` and `gen-features-page` rebuild these from sources already
# in the repo — measured 2026-09-30 at 21.1s for all four, with every input tracked and `gh`
# optional (it fails loudly and the page still writes). A committed copy is stale the moment its
# source moves, which is precisely the defect the `regen-*` hooks exist to prevent: a
# confident-looking page describing a world that has moved on. They are also 1–1.6MB of generated
# HTML, so every branch touching `docs/backlog.md` would conflict on them.
docs/explainers/dashboard.html
docs/explainers/dashboard.fragment.html
docs/explainers/goals.html
docs/explainers/goals.fragment.html
docs/explainers/backlog-table.html
docs/explainers/backlog-table.fragment.html
docs/explainers/features.html
docs/explainers/features.fragment.html
# The server's own runtime droppings — it writes these into whatever it serves.
docs/explainers/.serve.log
docs/explainers/.serve.pid

# Fixtures the scripts/check-surface-recall.py self-test writes into the REAL hooks directory.
# ⚠ THEY LIVE IN THE REPO ON PURPOSE AND THAT IS A TRADE, NOT AN OVERSIGHT — the hook derives
# REPO_ROOT from ${BASH_SOURCE[0]}, so a fixture under /tmp observes a repo that does not exist
# and an arm branching on a real repo file takes the wrong branch. Fidelity requires the real path.
# ⛔ THE FINALLY THAT REMOVES THEM DOES NOT RUN ON SIGKILL — reproduced at 3 of 13 kill offsets
# (backlog #212). This line is what stops the debris being committed by a `git add -A` when that
# happens. The suite also sweeps dead-pid leftovers on startup; this is the second layer.
# ⚠ THE PREFIX IS NOW HELD IN THREE PLACES (here, check-surface-recall.FIXTURE_PREFIX,
# check-ratchet-contract), because a consistent rename would otherwise orphan this line in
# silence. Backlog #215. ⛔ THE RECONCILER IS IN `check-surface-recall.main`, NOT IN ITS SUITE,
# and an earlier version of this very comment said "a self-test case reconciles this file" —
# WHICH WAS FALSE: every case passes text the case builds, and only `main` reads this file.
# That is backlog #216's defect — a comment asserting a defence the code does not implement —
# written in the commit that CLOSED #216. The claim is now what is true: `main` reads it, three
# cases drive `main` over a constructed .gitignore, and a mutation entry kills the wiring.
.claude/hooks/_selftest-*
